 "summary": "All four earlier proof-quality findings are fixed at the PR head. Dual-shift transport now uses `Multiset.forall_mem_map_iff` at both sites (Vertical.lean:320, 322, 597, 599). The normalization proof states the per-shift real-part equality as `hshift` (Specializations.lean:36) and no longer uses the nested `<;>` chain. The imaginary-part bound is the shared private `abs_im_sub_abs_im_le_abs_im_add` (Archimedean.lean:116, used at 311 and 354). `log_norm_gammaFactor` applies `Real.log_multiset_prod` once to the combined multiset (Basic.lean:175). I found no remaining issues with undocumented definitional-equality steps, brittle rewrite chains or oversized proofs.",
